st effective strategy is to attach the weak 8 to the strong triplet of Aces (AAA). This move clears 4 cards at once and removes the 8 safely. This leaves me with a hand of K, 2, Red Joker. Since I have the Red Joker and a 2, I can easily control the board when playing singles. I will likely play the K next; if it passes, I win. If it is beaten, I can use the 2 or Red Joker to regain the lead and finish the game. This path minimizes the number of turns and risks compared to playing the 8 as a single.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣8", "♠A", "♥A", "♣A"]}'}
